                <pb facs="0528" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg448"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.01/14</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1930-11-05"
                            >November 5, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received November 12.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 222</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    Peruvian Junta of Government on November first accorded recognition to the new
                    Junta of Government in Brazil, even before the latter had been formed.</p>
                <p>My Brazilian colleague informs me that the Peruvian Minister in Rio de Janeiro
                    accorded recognition through the Foreign Office two days before Getulio Vargas
                    took the oath as provisional President and the announcement of the composition
                    of his Cabinet.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fred Morris
                    Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
